            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Use species $A,B$, one reaction column $\\nu=(-1,1)^{\\mathsf T}$, and starting amounts $n_A^0=0$ mol, $n_B^0=1$ mol. The admissible extents are $\\xi\\in[-1,0]$ mol because $n_A(\\xi)=-\\xi$ and $n_B(\\xi)=1\\,\\mathrm{mol}+\\xi$ must both be nonnegative. Let $\\Phi_0$ have units joules and define an ambient affine potential on an open neighborhood of the nonnegative amount region by\n$$\n\\widehat\\Phi(n_A,n_B)=\\Phi_0+1\\,\\mathrm J-(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}})n_B .\n$$\nAlong $n(\\xi)=(-\\xi,1\\,\\mathrm{mol}+\\xi)$, set $\\Phi(\\xi):=\\widehat\\Phi(n(\\xi))=\\Phi_0-(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}})\\xi$. Its derivative-defined amount coefficients are $\\mu_A:=\\partial_{n_A}\\widehat\\Phi=0$ and $\\mu_B:=\\partial_{n_B}\\widehat\\Phi=-1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$, including at $\\xi_*=0$ mol. This ambient extension is constructed optimization data only; no positive-mole thermodynamic chart at $n_A=0$ or physical realization is asserted.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "6f3ba82a907a980d66ca5297fd6d5b4f39bd57dfdaa995d9b25fa145bf82ae14",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
