        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "one: The one boundary is outside the explicitly stated hypotheses or no such case is asserted.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $K=(-1,0)\\cup(0,1)$, which is noncompact: the open cover $U_n=(-1,-1/n)\\cup(1/n,1)$ for $n\\ge2$ has no finite subcover. Let $C=[-1,1]$ and use dimensionless coordinate $x$. For constants $s_0>a>0$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, define the ambient entropy extension and its restriction by\n$$\n\\widetilde s(x)=s_0-a x^2\\quad(x\\in C),\\qquad s=\\widetilde s|_K.\n$$\nFor $x,y\\in C$ and $t\\in[0,1]$,\n$$\n\\widetilde s((1-t)x+ty)=(1-t)\\widetilde s(x)+t\\widetilde s(y)+a t(1-t)(x-y)^2\\ge(1-t)\\widetilde s(x)+t\\widetilde s(y),\n$$\nso $\\widetilde s$ is concave on the convex ambient domain. It is continuous, bounded, and positive since $s_0-a>0$. The admissible generator set $K$ excludes the maximizing point $x=0$. Declare all Borel probability measures on $K$ with fixed barycenter $\\bar x=0$ feasible, with entropy per mole $\\int_Ks\\,dP$. For $y\\in K$, define the point mass $\\delta_y(A)=1$ if $y\\in A$ and $0$ otherwise for every Borel set $A\\subseteq K$. It is countably additive because at most one set in a disjoint family can contain $y$, and $\\delta_y(K)=1$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "e00ebac861533814d5157b313985e7a17608071580526c49981aa97985e21b3c",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
