          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "pthm-td-compact-continuous-phase-mixture",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $d\\ge1$ and let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty compact set of dimensionless generator coordinates. Each $x\\in K$ labels one model-specified phase-generator state; the model assigns it entropy per mole $s(x)\\in\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, and $s:K\\to\\mathbb R$ is continuous, using the numerical entropy value in that fixed unit. Define $\\operatorname{conv}K$ to be the set of all finite convex combinations of points of $K$, and fix $\\bar x\\in\\operatorname{conv}K$. Use the Borel sigma algebra relative to $K$. A Borel probability mixture is a countably additive probability measure $P$ on that sigma algebra; its barycenter and entropy per mole are the coordinatewise integrals $\\int_Kx\\,dP$ and $\\int_Ks\\,dP$. For $x\\in K$, define the unit point mass $\\delta_x$ by $\\delta_x(A)=1$ if $x\\in A$ and $\\delta_x(A)=0$ otherwise, for Borel $A\\subseteq K$. Assume every Borel probability mixture with barycenter $\\bar x$ is feasible and has entropy per mole $\\int_Ks\\,dP$. Then there are $m\\le d+1$, points $x_1,\\ldots,x_m\\in K$, and weights $\\theta_i\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{i=1}^m\\theta_i=1$ such that $P_*:=\\sum_{i=1}^m\\theta_i\\delta_{x_i}$ is a feasible Borel probability mixture and $\\int_Ks\\,dP_*\\ge\\int_Ks\\,dP$ for every feasible mixture $P$.\n\nHere integrals use the measure convention of [[def-tdmath-measure-integral]]. The entropy map is part of the model; this theorem derives neither its microscopic meaning nor compactness of a physical phase domain.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-borel-sigma-algebra",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal T)$ be a topological space ([[def-topological-space]]). The\n**Borel sigma-algebra of $X$** is the sigma-algebra generated by its open sets:\n\n$$\\mathcal B(X):=\\sigma_X(\\mathcal T).$$\n\nIts members are the **Borel subsets** of $X$. The generated sigma-algebra exists\nand is minimal by [[thm-generated-sigma-algebra-exists-and-is-minimal]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
