          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Example",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $K=\\{0,1\\}\\subset\\mathbb R$ be the compact generator domain, with dimensionless coordinate $x$. On the convex ambient domain $[0,1]$, define the affine extension $\\widetilde s(x)=s_0+a x$ and restrict it to $s=\\widetilde s|_K$, where fixed $s_0,a>0$ have units $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$. For $x,y\\in[0,1]$ and $t\\in[0,1]$, $\\widetilde s((1-t)x+ty)=(1-t)\\widetilde s(x)+t\\widetilde s(y)$, so the extension is concave. Take the barycenter to be $\\bar x=\\tfrac12$ and declare every Borel probability mixture on $K$ with that barycenter feasible.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "51c45a2a9cffd742612f4327717c85d7e812b471c84fd0f60408f57a738f0b85",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
