      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain",
          "carrier": "items/def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain.md",
          "status": "current draft supplier; exact interface inspected, independent acceptance not asserted",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Fix a constitution $c$ with $C\\ge1$ named species and its equilibrium state domain $D_c\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{C+2}$ from [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. An interior composition is represented by\n\n$$\nx=(x_1,\\ldots,x_{C-1})\\in\\Delta_{C-1}^{\\circ}:=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^{C-1}:x_i>0,\\ \\sum_{i=1}^{C-1}x_i<1\\},\n$$\n\nwith $x_C:=1-\\sum_{i<C}x_i>0$; for $C=1$, $\\mathbb R^0=\\{0\\}$ and $x_1=1$.\n\nA **phase branch** $\\alpha$ is model data consisting of an open chart $W_\\alpha\\subseteq(0,\\infty)\\times\\mathbb R\\times\\Delta_{C-1}^{\\circ}\\times(0,\\infty)$ with coordinates $(T,p,x,m)$ and a $C^1$ diffeomorphism $\\sigma_\\alpha:W_\\alpha\\to U_\\alpha$ onto an open subset $U_\\alpha\\subseteq\\mathbb R^{C+2}$ contained in the equilibrium state domain $D_c$. Here $T$ is in kelvins, $p$ is in pascals, $m$ is total amount in moles, and $C^1$ means continuous first coordinate derivatives as in [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]. The chart dimension is $C+2$, matching the ambient dimension of $D_c$. At $\\sigma_\\alpha(T,p,x,m)$, the derivative-defined state functions of [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]] give temperature $T$, pressure $p$, and mole fractions $x_j=n_j/m$; here $n_{\\mathrm{tot}}:=\\sum_{i=1}^C n_i=m$ uses the finite-sum convention of [[def-finite-sum]]. An **intensive phase branch** additionally has each derivative-defined chemical potential $\\mu_j(T,p,x,m)$ independent of $m$ throughout $W_\\alpha$; write its value as $\\mu_j^\\alpha(T,p,x)$. This scale invariance is an explicit constitutive model property, not a consequence of [[post-td-bulk-additivity]]. A valid local response chart and its inverse are as in [[def-td-response-functions]] and [[def-td-legendre-potentials]]. Existence of $W_\\alpha$ or $\\sigma_\\alpha$ is a model premise, not a consequence of the equations of thermodynamics.\n\nOn a branch with a valid natural-variable chart, $G^\\alpha$ denotes the Gibbs potential of [[def-td-legendre-potentials]] restricted to the branch. For a one-component branch with amount $m_\\alpha>0$, define $g_\\alpha:=G^\\alpha/m_\\alpha$, $s_\\alpha:=S_\\alpha/m_\\alpha$, and $v_\\alpha:=V_\\alpha/m_\\alpha$, in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$, $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$, and $\\mathrm{m^3\\,mol^{-1}}$, respectively. These quotients need not be independent of amount, and $g_\\alpha=\\mu^\\alpha$ is not assumed by this definition. Such an equality requires a separate same-tag homogeneity hypothesis on the branch.\n\nA **phase mixture** of a finite list of branches is a feasible separated compound whose positive phase amounts $m_\\alpha$ have fractions $\\lambda_\\alpha:=m_\\alpha/\\sum_\\beta m_\\beta>0$ with $\\sum_\\alpha\\lambda_\\alpha=1$. Its extensive coordinates and entropy are those supplied by [[post-td-bulk-additivity]] and [[post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy]], on the exact feasible set of [[def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set]]. The mixture is in **coexistence** when it is an attained global entropy-maximizing endpoint under the declared totals and permitted exchanges, as in [[post-td-entropy-maximum]]. This definition does not assert that a maximum exists, that all branches can exchange every coordinate, or that metastable states are global equilibria.\n\nThe bulk scaling postulate may send a material tag $c$ to a different tag $c^{(\\lambda)}$. It therefore does not supply same-tag degree-one homogeneity of $G^\\alpha$ or $U^\\alpha$ on a phase branch. Any result using $g_\\alpha=\\mu^\\alpha$ must state that additional hypothesis.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[[def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain]] and [[post-td-bulk-additivity]]: For one component, the phase amounts add to $N$, and the separated phase volumes add to $V$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Definition/Postulate interface inspected; no proof obligation.",
          "consumer_use": "Used in 1.1."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "post-td-bulk-additivity",
          "carrier": "items/post-td-bulk-additivity.md",
          "status": "current draft supplier; exact interface inspected, independent acceptance not asserted",
          "source_section": "Postulate",
          "exact_statement": "Let $A$ and $B$ be two named subsystems with disjoint physical regions as in [[def-td-system-and-permitted-exchanges]], combined as a compound system $A\\sqcup B$ inside a declared outer boundary. The model's admitted separated pairs form a specified subset $\\mathcal C_{AB}\\subseteq D_A\\times D_B$ using [[def-subset-and-proper-subset]] and [[def-cartesian-product]]. For every pair $(x_A,x_B)\\in\\mathcal C_{AB}$, the composition map $\\kappa_{AB}:\\mathcal C_{AB}\\to D_{A\\sqcup B}$ is a function ([[def-function-space]]) adopted so the dimensioned coordinates of its output satisfy\n$$U_{A\\sqcup B}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=U_A(x_A)+U_B(x_B),\\qquad V_{A\\sqcup B}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=V_A(x_A)+V_B(x_B),\\qquad n_{A\\sqcup B,j}(\\kappa_{AB}(x_A,x_B))=n_{A,j}(x_A)+n_{B,j}(x_B).$$\nHere each coordinate function is the dimensioned map of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]] for its material constitution, with SI units as in [[def-td-si-quantities]].\n\nHere \u201cextensive coordinates\u201d means precisely the named coordinates declared additive by this postulate. Amount coordinates are aligned by species label; when a species is absent from one subsystem, its zero amount is in a separately declared composition boundary, not the positive-mole chart of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]]. This is an idealized composition rule: cross-interface and long-range interaction energy is omitted from $U_{A\\sqcup B}$, rather than asserted to vanish in nature. The postulate does not assert that every pair of subsystem states is physically admissible.\n\nThe framework's bulk family is a tagged family of material types. For each dimensionless scale $\\lambda>0$ the model may designate a tag $c^{(\\lambda)}$ and a subset $B_{c,\\lambda}\\subseteq D_c$ of states admitting a scaled copy, with inclusion as in [[def-subset-and-proper-subset]]. For $x=(\\hat U,\\hat V,\\hat n_1,\\ldots,\\hat n_r)\\in B_{c,\\lambda}$, the scaling map is the function $\\delta_\\lambda:B_{c,\\lambda}\\to D_{c^{(\\lambda)}}$ ([[def-function-space]]) given by $\\delta_\\lambda(x)=(\\lambda\\hat U,\\lambda\\hat V,\\lambda\\hat n_1,\\ldots,\\lambda\\hat n_r)$. The tag matters: $c^{(\\lambda)}$ is not silently identified with $c$. This postulate specifies the coordinate scaling model and energy additivity only; it does not postulate entropy additivity or exact scaling for every finite physical body.\n\nThis is an adopted physical composition rule, not a deduction from SI units or from the mathematics of Cartesian products.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[[def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain]] and [[post-td-bulk-additivity]]: For one component, the phase amounts add to $N$, and the separated phase volumes add to $V$.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current Definition/Postulate interface inspected; no proof obligation.",
          "consumer_use": "Used in 1.1."
        }
      ],
